## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about worst-case guarantees and practical trade-offs between quicksort and mergesort, including depth control, partition balance, and memory usage in a real-world data processing pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Hybrid sorting (introspective sort)
- Worst-case guarantees, space complexity
- Handling duplicates, stability considerations
- Practical performance on sorted/partially sorted data

## Code Example
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>

// Simplified hybrid sort: quicksort with depth limit, switch to mergesort when needed
int partition(std::vector<long long>& a, int l, int r) {
  long long pivot = a[(l + r) / 2];
  int i = l, j = r;
  while (i <= j) {
    while (a[i] < pivot) ++i;
    while (a[j] > pivot) --j;
    if (i <= j) std::swap(a[i++], a[j--]);
  }
  return i;
}

void mergeSort(std::vector<long long>& a, int l, int r, std::vector<long long>& tmp) {
  if (r - l <= 1) return;
  int m = (l + r) / 2;
  mergeSort(a, l, m, tmp);
  mergeSort(a, m, r, tmp);
  int i = l, j = m, k = 0;
  while (i < m || j < r) {
    if (j >= r || (i < m && a[i] <= a[j])) tmp[k++] = a[i++];
    else tmp[k++] = a[j++];
  }
  for (int t = 0; t < k; ++t) a[l + t] = tmp[t];
}

void hybridSort(std::vector<long long>& a, int l, int r, int depth, int depthLimit) {
  if (r - l <= 16) {
    std::sort(a.begin() + l, a.begin() + r + 1);
    return;
  }
  if (depth >= depthLimit) {
    std::vector<long long> tmp(r - l + 1);
    mergeSort(a, l, r + 1, tmp);
    return;
  }
  int p = partition(a, l, r);
  hybridSort(a, l, p - 1, depth + 1, depthLimit);
  hybridSort(a, p, r, depth + 1, depthLimit);
}

// Entry: call with depth=0 and depthLimit=2*log2(n)
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical graph DP with a real-world flavor (service startup), ensuring knowledge of cycle detection, topological order, and dynamic programming.

## Key Concepts

- Topological sort (Kahn/DFS)
- DAG DP for path/finish times
- Cycle detection via processed node count

## Code Example

```javascript
function earliestStartup(graph, startup, t) {
  const V = graph.length;
  const indeg = new Array(V).fill(0);
  for (let u = 0; u < V; u++) for (const v of graph[u]) indeg[v]++;
  const q = [];
  const earliest = startup.slice();
  for (let i = 0; i < V; i++) if (indeg[i] === 0) q.push(i);
  let seen = 0;
  while (q.length) {
    const u = q.shift();
    seen++;
    for (const v of graph[u]) {
      earliest[v] = Math.max(earliest[v], earliest[u] + startup[v]);
      if (--indeg[v] === 0) q.push(v);
    }
  }
  if (seen !== V) throw new Error('cycle detected');
  return earliest[t];
}
```

